/E (The SafetYetu training focused on essential skills such as situational awareness, assertiveness, and physical self-defense, empowering participants to better navigate potentially dangerous situations. Eng. Juliana highlighted the importance of keen observation and risk assessment, enabling individuals to recognize threats before they escalate. Participants learned to communicate assertively, using verbal strategies to set boundaries and address uncomfortable encounters confidently. The practical self-defense techniques tools were designed to empower individuals to protect themselves in threatening situations, thus reducing their vulnerability to sexual harassment and other forms of violence. By including young girls and women, the SafetYetu training aims to foster a generation that feels empowered to advocate for their safety and that of others in their communities.)
/Pg 21 0 R
