>>
endobj
371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 188 0 R
/E (To understand the impact of the Elimika na Mwajuma project, it is important to recognize the challenges faced by schools in addressing Sexual and Gender Based Violence cases . Many teachers lacked the skills and tools needed to support students dealing with trauma and sensitive cases. Stigma surrounding SGBV often discouraged students from seeking help, leaving them vulnerable and unsupported. The Elimika na Mwajuma: Championing for Safe Institutions \(Schools\) project aims to create safer school environments by transforming teachers into mentors who can effectively support students, handle cases by providing guidance and counseling to students who are facing challenges including victims of sexual and gender based violence or at risk. OVAH trained 10 teachers from Kwembe, Mnazi Mmoja, Tandika, Kivule, and Mashujaa Secondary Schools, and equipped them with the skills to handle SGBV cases by providing guidance and counseling to students, and legal support referrals. Throughout the program OVAH involved both teachers and students in various activities such as storytelling competitions which enhanced the awareness and action against Sexual and Gender Based Violence.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
