/E (During the session, the OVAH team shared the inspiration behind the character Mwajuma, the central figure of the animation series. Mwajuma symbolizes the experiences of many girls in the community who are survivors of sexual and gender-based violence. Key themes such as rape, grooming, and victim-blaming were explored to ensure students understood the importance of these issues and how to convey them effectively in their stories. The workshop also emphasized the role of teachers, mentored by OVAH, in providing guidance and counseling to support survivors of GBV.)
/Pg 26 0 R
