/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (Sexual harassment is alarmingly prevalent worldwide, and Tanzania is no exception. Women and girls in Tanzania face daily incidents of catcalling, inappropriate touching, and other forms of harassment, with public spaces especially public transit serving as major hotspots for such violations. A 2022 study on sexual harassment in public transport among female university students in Dar es Salaam revealed an 88% prevalence, with verbal harassment being the most reported form \(95%\). Despite legal protections under the Sexual Offenses Special Provisions Act \(1998\) and the Employment and Labour Relations Act \(2004\), enforcement remains a significant challenge. The perception of these incidents as harmless or minor perpetuates a culture that enables sexual abuse and exploitation.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
