/P 200 0 R
/E (Throughout the months of February and March, we addressed critical issues impacting Tanzanian youth through our monthly episodes of the Orange Table Series. We explored intimate partner violence \(IPV\), emphasizing early intervention and community support. In the realm of online safety, we focused on digital literacy, parental guidance, and reporting mechanisms. Additionally, we tackled the persistence of sexual harassment in public spaces, advocating for awareness campaigns, youth engagement, and collective action. Our call to action includes staying informed, educating others, advocating for safer spaces, and being allies. If you or someone you know needs a safe and confidential space to share experiences and knowledge, The Orange Table Series is here for you.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
465 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (Mental health is a basic human right. According to World Health Organization WHO, Mental health is defined as a state of mental well-being that enables people to cope with the stresses of life, realize their abilities, learn well and work well, and contribute to their community.When considering Survivors of Sexual and Gender-based Violence, Mental health takes on even greater significance due to the profound impact these experiences have on their well-being. Survivors are at an increased risk for depression, anxiety, substance misuse disorders, post-traumatic stress disorder \(PTSD\), and even suicide attempts. The trauma they endure can disrupt their emotional equilibrium, leaving lasting scars.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
466 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (With survivors of Sexual Gender-based Violence \(SGBV\) at the heart of our programs, on Friday, May 31st, we hosted an impactful episode of the Orange Table Series. In this episode, we focused on supporting the mental well-being of Survivors of Sexual Violence. We invited a group of expert mental health aiders, psychologists, and therapists to join us in an Instagram Live session. Together, we aimed to unravel and break the chains of silence and stigma associated with seeking and providing mental health support.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
