/E (During the forum, OVAH contributed to the panel discussion focused on the third intervention pillar: Preventing Physical, Sexual, and Emotional Violence. Modesta Joseph OVAH's Founder, shared effective strategies for strengthening protection systems to improve responses and support for adolescent victims of violence. She highlighted OVAH's school-based awareness programs and shared success stories from the "Teachers to Mentors" project which creates safe spaces in schools and fosters mentorship between teachers and students. Modesta also discussed ongoing challenges, such as underfunded protection systems, fragmented services, and untrained personnel, which lead to inadequate responses and re-victimization. She emphasized the need for continuous improvements, along with adolescent participation and co-creation, to drive meaningful change in the community.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (The forum also provided a platform for adolescents and stakeholders to openly discuss the challenges they encounter and shared several recommendations to tackle them. Conclusively, stakeholders recommended ensuring a consistent project coordination across all levels, and establishing regular evaluation strategies to assess intervention effectiveness and consider a potential second phase NAIA-AHW strategy.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
