/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (Ending Sexual and Gender Based Violence requires collective action, and through this painting , OVAH invites parents, teachers, local authority leaders \(government\), and community members in general to reflect on their roles in fostering a safer environment for all. The painting emphasizes the importance of reporting of SGBV cases . OVAH has 2 teachers from teachers to mentors who provide guidance and counseling to students who are victims or at risk to face SGBV. Through this paint we aim to see more students seeking help and break the culture of silence that often surrounds such issues.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
530 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (During the unveiling of the painting, the OVAH team, along with teachers and students, pledged their support for ending SGBV by putting their colored palms in the wall. This collective commitment stands as a permanent testament that everyone has a role to play in this fight. Together we can create a community where schools are safe spaces for learning and growth.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
